# {{name}}

An Axum service built with [Ferrum Alloy](https://github.com/ferrum-edge/ferrum-alloy).
Handlers in `src/lib.rs` are ordinary Axum. Alloy adds configuration, Problem Details errors, health endpoints, limits, graceful shutdown, and request telemetry.

## Run

```bash
cargo run
curl -s localhost:8080/hello
curl -s localhost:8080/readyz
curl -s -X POST localhost:8080/items -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"name":"tea","quantity":2}'
```

Management endpoints listen on `127.0.0.1:9090`. `/livez` and `/readyz` are
minimal token-free probes. `/health`, `/metrics`, and management OpenAPI/UI
require `Authorization: Bearer <token>` even on loopback; without a configured
token they return `401`. Set `FERRUM_ALLOY_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN_FILE` to a file
containing a secret of at least 32 characters. Keep the file readable only by
the service account (for example, mode `0600` on Unix), and do not put a live
token in `alloy.toml` or a URL. A browser does not add bearer tokens itself;
for the management UI, use a local proxy or a carefully scoped header-injecting
extension that reads the token from a protected source. Diagnostic retrieval,
when enabled, has a separate authorizer; the management token does not grant
access to it. See the [management and secrets guide](https://github.com/ferrum-edge/ferrum-alloy/blob/main/docs/configuration.md#management).

## Test

```bash
cargo test
```

## Check configuration

```bash
ferrum-alloy check --config alloy.toml
```
